<%# One feed/profile/thread entry (ledger redesign, 2026-10): the row and,
    for a root pulse, its inline thread frame as SIBLINGS — empty until
    opened, or pre-filled through `thread_content` (the deep-link page) —
    so a drop broadcast that replaces #pulse_N leaves an open thread
    alone, while delete removes #pulse_N_entry whole. Prepend (feed) and
    append (thread list) broadcasts render this partial.
    Locals: pulse (required); viewer, echoed, indicator, indicator_alias,
    pinnable, pinned, can_up, can_down, in_thread, parent, reply_count
    (see pulse_row); thread_content. %>
<%
  thread = !pulse.is_splice?
  row_locals = local_assigns.slice(:viewer, :echoed, :indicator, :indicator_alias, :pinnable, :pinned,
    :can_up, :can_down, :in_thread, :parent, :reply_count)
  row_locals[:thread_frame] = "pulse_#{pulse.id}_thread" if thread
%>
<div id="pulse_<%= pulse.id %>_entry" class="wire-entry" data-at="<%= (pulse.pulsed_at.to_f * 1000).to_i %>">
  <%= render "wire/pulse_row", pulse: pulse, **row_locals %>
  <% if thread %>
    <%= turbo_frame_tag "pulse_#{pulse.id}_thread", class: "wire-thread", target: "_top" do %><%= local_assigns[:thread_content] %><% end %>
  <% end %>
</div>
